{"name":"Goose Bill","hex":"#ffba80","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grazing waterfowl of the family Anatidae, which have feathers and webbed feet and are capable of flying, swimming, and walking on land, and which are generally bigger than ducks.","A female goose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sharply poke or pinch the buttocks, or prod between the buttocks (of a person).","To stimulate; to spur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose"},{"term":"bill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written list or inventory. (Now obsolete except in specific senses or set phrases; bill of lading, bill of goods, etc.)","A document, originally sealed; a formal statement or official memorandum. (Now obsolete except with certain qualifying words; bill of health, bill of sale etc.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To advertise by a bill or public notice.","To charge; to send a bill to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose","wikidata":"Q16529344"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp